Chapter 9
I feel my whole body aching. I'm sweating even though I feel cold.
(t): What was that? I don't feel so good.
I hear some muffled voices and then the click of a door opening.
Miss Moon: On second thought, just leave it here. I'll take care of it myself.
???: But you mustn't, my lady! It is my duty—
Miss Moon: It's fine, Amelie.
Amelie: As you wish, my lady.
(t): Miss Moon? Who's Amelie? Am I having a weird dream again?
Just when I am about to open my eyes, I feel something cold on my forehead.
Me: Mm!
(t): That startled me!
Miss Moon: Sorry, did I wake you up?
I blink a few times.
I notice that I'm lying in a big and comfy bed, and Miss Moon just placed a wet towel on my forehead.
The interior of the room I'm in looks pretty lavish, decorated in rococo style.
Me: Where am I? What happened, Miss Moon?
I now notice that my boss looks completely different than what I'm used to.
(t): She's wearing a dress? And her eyes are different. They're both blue now. Was she really just wearing one contact lens then?
Miss Moon: Sigh, how will I even begin to explain this?
Then I notice what's probably the biggest difference.
(t): Her scar is gone???
Me: Huh? Miss Moon! Y—Your scar…
I try to sit up but sink back down after being hit with a wave of dizziness.
Miss Moon: You should stay put in bed for now. You're sick.
(t): Yeah, I can feel it.
Miss Moon: First of all, please call me Lady Scarlet… or just Scarlet from now on.
(t): Call her by her first name?? Wait, what's with the “lady”?
Me: What do you mean, Miss M—
Miss Moon: None of that! You cannot say that here under any circumstances, understood?
Me: Okay, uh… S—Scarlet.
Scarlet: Good. Now listen to me. I know it might be hard to believe, but it seems we've travelled back in time. We're in the house I grew up in.
CHOICE OPTION 1: How am I supposed to believe that?
(t): This is unbelievable.
Me: What are you talking about? If we really travelled back, shouldn't we be younger? Or did we not travel back that far? But everything seems so antique in here.
Scarlet: I know how surreal this seems, but we really did travel back in time. I cannot answer the question regarding your age, but you can clearly see that this environment is from another era. Also, you pointed out my missing scar yourself.
(t): She's right about that...
Scarlet continues mumbling something.
Scarlet: I don't know if it has anything to do with all the nightmares I've been having recently.
(t): That reminds me. Maybe it isn't that strange after all. I've been having some weird experiences myself lately.
Me: Okay. I believe you. But I wonder what happened earlier.
Scarlet: Hmm. We were in the office and somehow ended up here. I don't know…
She looks at me as if she's waiting for me to confess something.
CHOICE OPTION 2: Actually, I believe you.
Me: I've experienced some weird stuff myself, so this isn't really that hard to believe.
Scarlet looks surprised.
Scarlet: Really? That's good then. I was worried that I would have to answer a lot of questions from you.
Me: Don't get me wrong, I do have a lot of questions. Like, why can't I call you Miss Moon?
Scarlet: There is an explanation for that, but it's a really long one. I have questions myself. I don't know what exactly happened for us to end up like this.
We both look at each other for a moment, not knowing what to say.
CONTINUE HERE AFTER CHOICE OPTIONS
Me: And how did we get here exactly?
Scarlet: That's what I want to ask you, actually.
Me: What do you mean? You think I did this?
Scarlet: Well, did you not? Because I know that it was for sure not me.
(t): Wait, is it really because of me? Did I somehow pull her into some kind of strange situation? Like what happened on my first day at the company when the building was warping around?
Me: I… am not quite sure. I just remember fainting after falling to the ground. Together with yo— UGH!
My head starts to hurt, and I am once again reminded of how sick my body is right now.
Scarlet: Right. I must have overworked you. Sorry about that… For now, get some rest. Amelie, my maid, will bring you some porridge later. Let's discuss this when you're better.
Me: But I have so many questions left.
Scarlet stands up and turns to the door.
Scarlet: I'll answer them all tomorrow. Good Night.
She leaves the room, and I am left alone with all the confusion in my head.
Soon after the maid comes by and I finish the porridge, I drift into sleep, letting my tired body and mind rest.
The next day I am woken up by Amelie.
Amelie: Good morning. Are you feeling better?
She opens the curtains and lets the sunlight flood into the room.
Me: Yes. I was able to rest comfortably, thank you.
(t): My fever and headache are completely gone. It must be because the bed is so soft. I slept like a log.
Amelie: I'm glad. I will tell Lady Scarlet. Someone will take you to eat breakfast with the Lady so please wait here for a moment.
Me: Okay.
(t): She's referred to as a lady again. What's her status exactly?
Amelie bows and leaves the room.
Before I can decide what to do next, two new women in maid uniforms enter the room.
Without talking much, they help me wash up and get ready.
They even help me get dressed.
(t): I've never worn clothes like these before. They seem similar in fashion to what Scarlet was wearing last night.
After that, I am led to a room where Scarlet is already waiting while sipping some tea.
Amelie is preparing a set of cutlery for me as I sit down across from Scarlet.
In front of us, there are various breakfast dishes spread out on the table.
(t): How extravagant.
Scarlet: I want to have a private conversation with my guest. You may leave.
The servants all bow and leave the room.
Me: So, what exactly is all this? Who are you?
Scarlet sighs.
Scarlet: I guess I have to tell you a secret of mine now. As you may have noticed, we are several hundred years in the past. We are in my childhood home right now.
(t): This doesn't really make sense. But it really looks like it.
Me: I get that we travelled back in time somehow, but how is this your childhood when we're talking about centuries here? Did you reincarnate and remember your past life? Or are you just an extremely old hag?
Her eyebrow twitches.
(t): Oops, I should watch my mouth.
Me: Sorry. Forget that last part.
Scarlet: Ahem. I shall explain everything to you. It might take a while, but it might help us assess the situation. Are you willing to listen and share information that might help us as well?
I nod with a serious look on my face.
This might help explain some of the things I've been wondering about.
Scarlet: Please, feel free to eat to your heart's content while we're at it.
(t): Can I really? What if I make a fool of myself again?
CHOICE OPTION 1: I'll just drink some tea with dignity.
I see that my cup has been filled with tea already. The servants probably did that.
Me: Thank you, but I normally don't have breakfast. This tea is enough.
I see something like disappointment appear on Scarlet's face for a brief moment, but it fades away quickly.
Scarlet: Okay then, I will just get right to it, I guess.
CHOICE OPTION 2: Whatever, I'm hungry. It would be rude to refuse.
Me: Thank you, it all looks so delicious.
(t): Wow, that egg dish looks scrumptious. Oh, or that one with the fluffy-looking bread. Or should I try that soup with the vibrant colour? Agh, there are too many choices!
Scarlet notices my eyes darting around, inspecting every dish carefully, unable to decide where to start.
Scarlet: Just try a bit of everything. Our cook is really good, so I'm sure you'll like it.
Me: Ah, then I will do that.
I begin to load my plate and don't even notice Scarlet chuckling.
ILLUSTRATION
I stuff my face with all the delightful dishes and finally notice her smiling.
I'm taken aback at how beautiful her smiling face is.
Scarlet: I'm glad I'm able to share this food with someone. They're all my favourites. I'm happy you like them.
(t): Gulp.
Me: Pretty.
Scarlet: Hm?
Me: I mean, uh, delicious! I really like it.
(t): Ahhhh! Why did I say that??
Hoping that she didn't hear that, I try to brush over it.
Me: So, what's your story?
Scarlet's face turns somewhat serious again.
Scarlet: Right, I should get to the point.
CONTINUE HERE AFTER CHOICE OPTION
Scarlet finishes the last bit of her tea and puts the cup down before she finally begins to talk.
Scarlet: I grew up here as the only daughter of the duke. In two months from here, I will enter an arranged marriage with the crown prince.
My eyes widen with surprise.
(t): She will be a princess?
Scarlet: We returned right back to where my life began to unravel into chaos. But we're already at the point of no return. This marriage will lead to a tragedy that will haunt me for the rest of my life.
Me: What do you mean?
Scarlet: If things continue like they did in the past, then I will end up being a murderer.
I gasp and cover my mouth with my hand in shock.
Me: That means… you're a murderer? Like, even when I got to know you at the company, you were already a murderer?
Scarlet: Unfortunately, yes. And I don't want to go through that again, so I'm hoping that either we will be able to return to the present soon or that I can change the events in a way so that I won't have to kill anyone.
(t): Have to?
Me: Wait, it sounds to me like the murder wasn't exactly something you planned. So, if I may ask, what was the reason, and who did you kill?
She looks away with a saddened expression.
Scarlet: The crown prince was… no, is a deceiving cheater. And well, things happened after I found out… I don't really want to recall all those memories, to be honest. But aren't you curious about something else?
Me: Hm?
(t): Honestly, I can't imagine my boss murdering someone for real, but I can't help but imagine the whole scenario. Especially since we're talking about a crown prince.
(t): Oh, now that I think about it, how was she able to live such a long life?
Me: Right, how did you make it to the present? You look a lot younger than a few centuries old.
Scarlet: This might come as another surprise to you, but… I am a vampire. We age differently than normal humans.
It's quiet for a few seconds.
(t): Like, the ones who bite the necks of people to drink their blood? Like in the movies?
Suddenly, her killing a person doesn't seem that shocking anymore.
Me: But, you don't seem like a bloodthirsty monster to me.
She is about to take another sip of her tea but stops moving after my statement.
She then gives me a piercing look and I flinch at the sight.
(t): Her eyes are red!
Scarlet: I constantly hide my true form, I've learned to do so when I was still a child. But when I get too agitated or can't properly control it, then my true form reveals itself.
She points to her very pointy canines before proceeding to drink from her teacup.
(t): Woah… That's kind of cool… but also a little scary.
Me: That's amazing! I don't think I could do that.
Scarlet: What's so amazing about that? It's just like learning how to walk when you're a child.
(t): If I'm not mistaken, I can see her blushing a little.
Me: I mean, I thought you were amazing even before I knew about you being a vampire. You are a hardworking boss and I can feel that you really care about the company.
She turns her head to the side and avoids my gaze, but I can see how red her ear is.
Me: And now that I know how long you've lived, I can only imagine what hardships you had to go through to stay hidden and not raise any suspicions. I respect you even more now.
Scarlet: Stop.
Me: Hm?
(t): Did I say something wrong?
Scarlet: It's the first time I hear someone talk like that about a blood sucking monster. You certainly are a weird one.
I chuckle at the sight of an embarrassed Scarlet.
(t): Wait, if she drinks blood, does that mean…
Me: So, you need blood to survive, right?
Scarlet: Yes.
Me: Blood… of a h-human?
Scarlet: Yes.
(t): How can she just admit that? Do I have to worry about my safety?…
Scarlet: Don't worry. Most vampires don't attack humans. We have other means to get our hands on blood. We can also survive on animal blood for a while.
My shoulders relax a bit.
Me: Okay, then I'll take your word for it.
Scarlet: Most humans react in fear if they find out about vampires existing, and a lot resort to violence without even hearing our side out. That's why we have to hide the fact that we're vampires from the public eye. Even the crown prince didn't know that he was supposed to get married to a vampire.
Me: That's understandable. The crown prince. He's still alive, right?
Scarlet just nods wordlessly.
(t): Wait, that means…
Me: Then we can undo your mistake of murdering him! Then you won't be troubled by that anymore.
